# Testing and validation

Do not claim completion because the app compiles. `ignoreBuildErrors` / `ignoreDuringBuilds` in Next config do not waive validation.

## What to run (as applicable)

- TypeScript and ESLint on files you touched (do not “fix the world”)
- Vitest: `apps/hospital-portal-web/src/**/*.test.ts(x)` — colocate new unit tests with the lib/component
- Existing integration tests / backend tests when APIs or schema are in scope (schema/API changes themselves need explicit approval)
- Playwright: **active suite is `apps/hospital-portal-web/e2e/`** (`playwright.config.ts` `testDir: ./e2e`)
- Do **not** treat `apps/hospital-portal-web/tests/e2e/` or repo-root `tests/` as the live suite (legacy paths)
- Accessibility checks (keyboard, focus, dialogs, labels)
- Browser verification of the real workflow, not a single screenshot

Keep `ip-overlays-consolidated.test.ts` green for IP overlays.

## Playwright / browser

For UI changes verify: route load, authz, patient/encounter context, primary workflow, keyboard, dialogs/drawers, forms, validation, errors, loading, responsive, a11y.

Use safe UAT/seed data. Do not perform destructive production actions. Preserve existing ward-journey / census / CCMS / counselling / patient-hub projects and storageState setup.

## Figma / visual

When a Figma URL exists, follow `.cursor/rules/figma-mcp.mdc`: remote MCP only; `figma-design-to-code` then `get_design_context`; map to existing portal components/tokens; **do not** paste generated Tailwind as a new design system; **do not** recreate mockup HTML as production.

Then: inspect existing screen → implement with canonical components → run the app → Playwright/browser → compare → fix → check responsive states. Mockups under `apps/hospital-portal-web/docs/mockups/` are reference, not a second app.

## Reports and analytics

Reporting UIs must not mutate transactional data. Tests should not require writing production bills/claims to “see a chart.”

## Cross-module

If you change shared `ui/*`, patient context, billing payment, or SignalR helpers, search consumers and re-validate affected modules (queue, ward, OT, cashier, CCMS, exam, portal as relevant).
